{"strongs": "H2677", "word": "חֲצִי", "translit": "che.tsi", "root": "חפף", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "half", "definition": "חֲצִי 123 noun masculine Num 12:12 half (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician חצי ; on formative see Lag BN 113 ) — absolute חֲצִי 1Kgs 3:25 (twice in verse) + 3 t.; הַחֵ֑צִי 1Kgs 10:7 , compare 1Kgs 16:21 וָחֵ֔צִי Ezek 40:42 וָחֵצִי Dan 12:7 + 13 t. (usually with Pashta or Tiphcha), compare בַּחֵ֖צִי 2Sam 10:4 ; 1Chr 19:4 construct חֲצִי Exod 12:29 + 84 t.; suffix חֶצְיוֺ Exod 38:4 + 7 t. + Josh 8:33 וְהַחֶצְיוֺ (but article suspicious. see Ges «GKC:127»§ 127 R 3, 4); חֶצְיָהּ Neh 3:38 חֶצְיֵנוּ 2Sam 18:3 חֶצְיָם Zech 14:8 (twice in verse) + 2 t. — 1. half of anything: — blood of offering Exod 24:6 (twice in verse) ( J E ), beard 2Sam 10:4 , a hin Num 15:9 ; Num 15:10 ; Num 28:14 ( P ); curtain Exod 26:12 ( P ); week השׁבוע ׳ ח Dan 9:27 etc.; אַמָּה ׳ ח half a cubit Exod 26:16 ; Exod 36:21 ( P ) +; especially שׁבט ׳ ח half a tribe Num 32:33 ; Num 34:13 ; Num 34:14 ; Num 34:15 ( P ) +; half of people 2Sam 18:3 ; 2Sam 19:41 ; 1Kgs 16:21 (3 t. in verse) +, etc. so הַמְּנֻחוֺת ׳ ח 1Chr 2:52 and הַמָּנַחְתִּי ׳ ח v 1Chr 2:54 (see Be and מָנַחַת below נוח ). — On כבחצי 1Sam 14:4 see We Dr . 2. middle הלילה ׳ ח Exod 12:29 ( J ) midnight , so Judg 16:3 (twice in verse); Ruth 3:8 of garments 2Sam 10:4 ; 1Chr 19:4 altar Exod 27:5 of the Mt. of Olives Zech 14:4 יָמַי ׳ ח Ps 102:25 the midst of my days (when they are but half done), Jer 17:11 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3031')\">BDB3031</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2677')\">H2677</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3030')\">BDB3030</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3032')\">BDB3032</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חֲצִי</bdbheb><sub>123</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Num 12:12\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(4,12,12)\">Num 12:12</ref></sup> <highlightword>half</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Phoenician <bdbheb>חצי</bdbheb>; on formative see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>BN 113</sup></lookup>) — absolute <bdbheb>חֲצִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 3:25\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(11,3,25)\">1Kgs 3:25</ref> (twice in verse) + 3 t.; <bdbheb>הַחֵ֑צִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 10:7\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(11,10,7)\">1Kgs 10:7</ref>, compare <ref ref=\"1Kgs 16:21\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(11,16,21)\">1Kgs 16:21</ref> <bdbheb>וָחֵ֔צִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 40:42\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"42\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"42\" onclick=\"bcv(26,40,42)\">Ezek 40:42</ref> <bdbheb>וָחֵצִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Dan 12:7\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(27,12,7)\">Dan 12:7</ref> + 13 t. (usually with Pashta or Tiphcha), compare <bdbheb>בַּחֵ֖צִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 10:4\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(10,10,4)\">2Sam 10:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 19:4\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(13,19,4)\">1Chr 19:4</ref> construct <bdbheb>חֲצִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 12:29\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(2,12,29)\">Exod 12:29</ref> + 84 t.; suffix <bdbheb>חֶצְיוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 38:4\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(2,38,4)\">Exod 38:4</ref> + 7 t. + <ref ref=\"Josh 8:33\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"33\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"33\" onclick=\"bcv(6,8,33)\">Josh 8:33</ref> <bdbheb>וְהַחֶצְיוֺ</bdbheb> (but article suspicious. see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:127»§ 127</sup> R 3, 4); <bdbheb>חֶצְיָהּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Neh 3:38\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(16,3,38)\">Neh 3:38</ref>